# A lens on the board's file: `pin` puts a Notice into the file and `posts` gets it back as the Posts the file holds, a
# Notice being a Post. The route of an exported class is its constructor and its public methods, in the order the class
# lists them, each called by the class's caller and run on the caller's Board; so the file stands between the put and
# the get. What a method gives, the constructor's Board among it, goes back to that caller, beyond the plan.

route club.files.Board
step Board()/Board()
step Board()/Board.pin
step Board()/Board.posts
step Board()/Board.posts/Notice()

line entry > Board()/Board() call
line entry > Board()/Board.pin call
line entry > Board()/Board.posts call
line Board()/Board() > Board@Board()/Board() value
line Board > Board()/Board.pin value # the caller's instance: every method runs on it
line Board > Board()/Board.posts value
line Notice·notice > Board()/Board.pin value # pin's parameter, by the name that holds it
line Board()/Board.pin > Disk(Board.path) own
line Disk(Board.path) > Board()/Board.posts own
line Board()/Board.posts/Notice() > Notice@Board()/Board.posts/Notice() value
line Notice@Board()/Board.posts/Notice() > Board()/Board.posts value   # posts hands back the Notice it built
line Board()/Board.posts > Post@Board()/Board.posts value        # as the Posts its signature gives

home Board@Board()/Board() Board()
home Board Board()
home Notice·notice Board()
home Notice@Board()/Board.posts/Notice() Board()/Board.posts
home Post@Board()/Board.posts Board()

side entry left
side Disk(Board.path) between
